; Output: PDR.M
; Console: PDR.OUT
; PMDMML.MAN §14-1, §15-2

#Title PDR
#Option /v/c

; §15-2 PDR operation mode control, interleaved with §14-1 rhythm shots. The
; rhythm part is where this command byte differs from the FM part's §9-3
; software LFO switch. The operands cover every (PDR number, mode) pair the
; driver receives, since the original splits the byte into AL = n >> 1 and
; DL = n & 1. 4 and 5 are the EI and DI modes.
K *0 \b *1 \s *2 \h *3 \t *4 \c *5 \i
